WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.408
The takeaway is simple.

00:00:01.488 --> 00:00:04.449
Squaring turns subtractive mixtures into valid,

00:00:04.529 --> 00:00:09.947
tractable probabilistic models that need
exponentially fewer components than additive

00:00:10.027 --> 00:00:12.341
mixtures for the same expressiveness.

00:00:12.421 --> 00:00:16.999
Along the way, this one framework unifies
square-root-of-density models,

00:00:17.079 --> 00:00:19.393
positive semi-definite kernel models,

00:00:19.473 --> 00:00:24.180
and quantum Born machines under a single
property-driven view of circuits,

00:00:24.260 --> 00:00:26.186
making subtraction a practical,

00:00:26.266 --> 00:00:30.520
first-class tool for compact and expressive
probabilistic modeling.
